-- ── story 4-5a: packing documents ────────────────────────────────────────
-- Generated by drizzle-kit (the three tables and their indexes — made IF NOT
-- EXISTS by hand, the 6-2a lint) and hand-amended: the fail-fast guard, every
-- CHECK (drizzle-kit is blind to them), the RLS policies with the 0041 client
-- clause, the email_messages widening and the post-migration probes
-- (`bun run db:generate` afterwards reports "No schema changes").
--
-- What changes:
--  * `order_packs` (A1) — a pack's document header: one live pack per order,
--    the frozen document parties, the carton count and the gross weight.
--  * `order_cartons` (A2) — one carton of one pack, its code tied to its row
--    (`order_cartons_code_derived`) and unique per tenant.
--  * `order_carton_lines` (A3) — one SKU in one carton (milli-units).
--  * `email_messages` (A4) — the `packing-slip-pdf` attachment kind, paired
--    with the `client-dispatch` template.
--
-- The three tables are new and empty, so every CHECK on them is added
-- validated. The two email_messages CHECKs are re-added validated over a
-- superset (asserted below), as 0116 did: the table is small (mail rows purge
-- at 90 days) and every existing row satisfies the wider set by construction.
-- Later migrations (4-6a 0118, 4-9a 0119, 4-10a 0120) drop and re-add these
-- constraints BY NAME — the names are a contract.
-- No foreign keys (IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE §3). Additive only: no backfill (a
-- pack written before this migration is read as a virtual pack, A9).

-- ── 0. fail-fast: already applied ───────────────────────────────────────
